<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albertine line</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Albertines</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Albertine line is the younger branch of the house of Wettin, founded by Duke Albert III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> when he and his brother Ernest divided their lands by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/division-of-leipzig">Division of Leipzig</a> in 1485. It held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meissen">Meissen</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a>, and in 1547 it gained the electoral title from the Ernestines. Its members ruled Saxony as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> and, from 1806 to 1918, as kings, and two were elected kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</p></div>
